<item>
<title>Telegram macOS</title>
<description>New:&lt;br&gt;• The brain in an AI task bubble can be grabbed and pulled until it tears&lt;br&gt;• Letters flying into the black hole while a conversation is compacted bend toward the pointer&lt;br&gt;• Photos, videos, files and other media are stored encrypted on this Mac&lt;br&gt;• Encrypted exports open in a browser with a password Telegram shows once&lt;br&gt;• A strength meter under a new passcode while you type it&lt;br&gt;• Widgets now run on Nova, a JavaScript engine in Rust with every unsafe operation removed for protection, so a widget's script can't corrupt memory; it runs inside the sandboxed widget process, and QuickJS no longer runs widget code&lt;br&gt;• The widget checker runs on Nova too, and the widget process refuses any other engine&lt;br&gt;• Beta updates now list what changed, taken from the pushed changes&lt;br&gt;• Widgets can be drawn in a separate sandboxed process as well (debug switch, off by default)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Improved:&lt;br&gt;• Widgets start as fast as before the new engine: its startup code is compiled once and shared&lt;br&gt;• A redesigned Optimizing Database screen that fades into your chats&lt;br&gt;• Widgets run about 30% faster on the new engine; heavy widgets are no longer stopped by the time limit&lt;br&gt;• A widget can no longer stall the widget process while its script is being read&lt;br&gt;• Stronger protection of local data: passcode-protected database key, encrypted AI assistant storage, Mini App secrets kept per account&lt;br&gt;• Telegram's local data is now always encrypted with a key kept in this Mac's Keychain, even without a passcode, so a copy of its files can't be read elsewhere&lt;br&gt;• Log Out on the passcode screen now erases the data stored on this Mac right away&lt;br&gt;• The passcode screen shows progress while it checks your passcode and pauses briefly after a wrong one&lt;br&gt;• Hovering a widget no longer makes Telegram parse the widget's HTML itself&lt;br&gt;• Widgets drawn in the separate process: smooth frames at the display's rate, steady while a message changes height, ready before they scroll into view, much less memory, animations at 60 frames a second, and a restart if that process ends&lt;br&gt;• Bot HTML documents, including tall ones and 3D, can be drawn in the separate process too (same debug switch)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fixed:&lt;br&gt;• The compacting black hole no longer flickers or gets cut off at the edges of its message&lt;br&gt;• Videos whose index points outside the file can no longer crash Telegram while seeking&lt;br&gt;• A widget can no longer crash the process that runs widgets, or go past its time and memory limits with regular expressions, typed arrays or huge BigInts&lt;br&gt;• A widget whose content kept its first size could stay waiting to appear&lt;br&gt;• Widgets whose code used a labelled block with break could silently skip the rest of their script&lt;br&gt;• Optimizing Database no longer appears every time Telegram is unlocked&lt;br&gt;• Widget animations no longer jump or stall: the process that runs widgets keeps full speed while a widget is on screen&lt;br&gt;• The passcode can be turned on again when the Keychain and the local data disagree about it&lt;br&gt;• Telegram crashed when the pointer left a widget drawn in the separate process&lt;br&gt;• Widgets drawn in the separate process showed older frames through transparent areas and blinked empty when coming back on screen&lt;br&gt;• Telegram no longer crashes when opening chats containing certain video files&lt;br&gt;• Seeking in videos, pausing or resuming recordings and calls are more reliable&lt;br&gt;</description>
<pubDate>2026-15-11 10:24:44</pubDate>
